{"content":[{"c":["AZARIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Very common Jewish name. Its numerous occurrences in the priestly genealogies has caused much confusion. The following is one of several possible arrangements:"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Zadok’s son or grandson. According to most translations, Azariah was high priest during Solomon’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.2","r":"1Kgs.4.2","rawR":"1Kgs.4.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.2","value":"1Kgs.4.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:2"},"). It is possible, however, that his position should be understood as that of a special counselor or keeper of the royal calendar."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Nathan’s son, a high official in King Solomon’s court. He was chief officer over the 12 regional administrators (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.5","r":"1Kgs.4.5","rawR":"1Kgs.4.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.5","value":"1Kgs.4.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Amaziah’s son, king of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.14.21","r":"2Kgs.14.21","rawR":"2Kgs.14.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.14.21","value":"2Kgs.14.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 14:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.15.1-7","r":"2Kgs.15.1-7","rawR":"2Kgs.15.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.15.1-7","value":"2Kgs.15.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:1-7"},"), more frequently known as Uzziah. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Uzziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Uzziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Uzziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Uzziah #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Ethan’s son, a descendant of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.8","r":"1Chr.2.8","rawR":"1Chr.2.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.8","value":"1Chr.2.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Jehu’s son, another descendant of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.38","r":"1Chr.2.38","rawR":"1Chr.2.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.38","value":"1Chr.2.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:38"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Ahimaaz’s son and Zadok’s grandson (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.9","r":"1Chr.6.9","rawR":"1Chr.6.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.9","value":"1Chr.6.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:9"},"). If Azariah #1 was indeed a high priest, this Azariah could be identified with him."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Johanan’s son and Amariah’s father (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.10-11","r":"1Chr.6.10-11","rawR":"1Chr.6.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.10-11","value":"1Chr.6.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:10-11"},"). He is identical with the Azariah of ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.3","r":"Ezra.7.3","rawR":"Ezra.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.3","value":"Ezra.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 7:3"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=2Esd.1.2","r":"2Esd.1.2","rawR":"2Esd.1.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Esd.1.2","value":"2Esd.1.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Esdras 1:2"},", whose father (meaning “ancestor”) was Meraioth. The parenthetical note about Solomon’s temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.10","r":"1Chr.6.10","rawR":"1Chr.6.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.10","value":"1Chr.6.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:10"},") is generally held to go with the Azariah of verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.9","r":"1Chr.6.9","rawR":"1Chr.6.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.9","value":"1Chr.6.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"9"}," (see #6 above). It is possible, however, that this Azariah served in the temple (built by Solomon) during the reign of Uzziah and is therefore identical with #17 below."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Hilkiah’s son and Seriah’s father (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.13-14","r":"1Chr.6.13-14","rawR":"1Chr.6.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.13-14","value":"1Chr.6.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:13-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.1","r":"Ezra.7.1","rawR":"Ezra.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.1","value":"Ezra.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Esd.1.1","r":"2Esd.1.1","rawR":"2Esd.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Esd.1.1","value":"2Esd.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Esd 1:1"},"). Some have identified this Azariah with #10 or #11 below."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Zephaniah’s son, an ancestor of the singer Heman. Heman sang in the worship ritual instituted by King David (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.36","r":"1Chr.6.36","rawR":"1Chr.6.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.36","value":"1Chr.6.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. Hilkiah’s son or descendant, one of the first priests to settle in Jerusalem after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","r":"1Chr.9.11","rawR":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.11","value":"1Chr.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:11"},"; “Seraiah,” ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.11","r":"Neh.11.11","rawR":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.11","value":"Neh.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Oded’s son, a prophet in the days of King Asa of Judah. He encouraged Asa to initiate badly needed reforms in the king’s 15th year (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.15.1-15","r":"2Chr.15.1-15","rawR":"2Chr.15.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.15.1-15","value":"2Chr.15.1-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 15:1-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12, 13. Two sons of King Jehoshaphat of Judah. Along with four of their brothers, they were killed for political reasons by Jehoram, heir to the throne (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.21.1-4","r":"2Chr.21.1-4","rawR":"2Chr.21.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.21.1-4","value":"2Chr.21.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 21:1-4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["14. Alternate name of Ahaziah, king of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.22.6","r":"2Chr.22.6","rawR":"2Chr.22.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.22.6","value":"2Chr.22.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 22:6"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Ahaziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Ahaziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Ahaziah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ahaziah #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["15. Jehoram’s son, one of Judah’s military commanders. This Azariah followed Jehoiada the priest in a rebellion that resulted in the execution of Queen Athaliah and the crowning of Joash as king (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.23.1","r":"2Chr.23.1","rawR":"2Chr.23.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.23.1","value":"2Chr.23.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 23:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["16. Obed’s son, another of the five commanders in league with Jehoiada against Athaliah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.23.1","r":"2Chr.23.1","rawR":"2Chr.23.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.23.1","value":"2Chr.23.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 23:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["17. High priest in Jerusalem during the reign of King Uzziah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.16-21","r":"2Chr.26.16-21","rawR":"2Chr.26.16-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.16-21","value":"2Chr.26.16-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:16-21"},"). He opposed Uzziah’s arrogant attempt to burn incense on the altar. Perhaps the same as #7 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["18. Johanan’s son, a leader of Ephraim’s tribe. Azariah and other leaders of the tribe joined the prophet Obed in protesting the capture of Judean prisoners by King Pekah of Israel and in effecting their release (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.28.12","r":"2Chr.28.12","rawR":"2Chr.28.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.28.12","value":"2Chr.28.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 28:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["19. Descendant of Kohath and the father of a Levite named Joel. Joel participated in the temple cleansing instituted by King Hezekiah of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.12","r":"2Chr.29.12","rawR":"2Chr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.12","value":"2Chr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["20. Jehallelel’s son. This Azariah, a descendant of Merari, also participated in Hezekiah’s cleansing of the temple (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.12","r":"2Chr.29.12","rawR":"2Chr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.12","value":"2Chr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["21. Zadok’s descendant and high priest during the reign of Hezekiah of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.31.10,13","r":"2Chr.31.10,13","rawR":"2Chr.31.10,13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.31.10,13","value":"2Chr.31.10,13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 31:10, 13"},"). He participated in Hezekiah’s massive religious reforms."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["22. Maaseiah’s son, a householder in Jerusalem who participated in Nehemiah’s rebuilding of the wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.23","r":"Neh.3.23","rawR":"Neh.3.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.23","value":"Neh.3.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["23. Leader who returned to Judah with Zerubbabel after the Babylonian exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.7","r":"Neh.7.7","rawR":"Neh.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.7","value":"Neh.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:7"},"; “Seraiah,” ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","r":"Ezra.2.2","rawR":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.2","value":"Ezra.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["24. Levitical assistant of Ezra who explained to the people passages from the law read by Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.8.7","r":"Neh.8.7","rawR":"Neh.8.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.8.7","value":"Neh.8.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 8:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["25. Priest who signed Ezra’s covenant of faithfulness to God with Nehemiah and others after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.2","r":"Neh.10.2","rawR":"Neh.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.2","value":"Neh.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["26. Participant in the dedication of the rebuilt wall of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.33","r":"Neh.12.33","rawR":"Neh.12.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.33","value":"Neh.12.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["27. Alternate form of Jaazaniah, the name of Hoshaiah’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.42.1","r":"Jer.42.1","rawR":"Jer.42.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.42.1","value":"Jer.42.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 42:1"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.43.2","r":"Jer.43.2","rawR":"Jer.43.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.43.2","value":"Jer.43.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:2"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jaazaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jaazaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jaazaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jaazaniah #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["28. One of the three young Jews taken into captivity with Daniel. In Babylon he was renamed Abednego (",{"href":"?bref=Dan.1.6-7,11,19","r":"Dan.1.6-7,11,19","rawR":"Dan.1.6-7,11,19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.1.6-7,11,19","value":"Dan.1.6-7,11,19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dn 1:6-7, 11, 19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Dan.2.17","r":"Dan.2.17","rawR":"Dan.2.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.2.17","value":"Dan.2.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:17"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=ShadrachMeshachandAbednego_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ShadrachMeshachandAbednego_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ShadrachMeshachandAbednego_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Azariah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.2","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.2","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.5","rawQuer